OpenBSD lacks xattrs; read symlink reparse data from regular files with
Wine's '?' suffix, matching server/fd.c.

Also: SYSCALL_NARROW_ARG() for the narrow (BOOLEAN/WORD) syscall
arguments in this file; see patch-include_wine_unixlib_h.

Directory reparse points: the data of a directory reparse point is kept
in .wine-reparse inside it (no extended attributes); read for "dir?/"
paths too, hidden from listings.

